        "problem": "Find $|r(2)|$ given that $r(t)=\u27e8t+1,\\,\\sqrt{t+1},\\,t\u27e9.$",
        "worked_solution": "Evaluating the function at $t=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(2) & =\u27e82+1,\\,\\sqrt{2+1},\\,2\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83,\\,\\sqrt{3},\\,2\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(2)| & =\\sqrt{(3)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+3+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
